IMPORT prelude

-- First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 (NT), with the First Home Owner Grant Regulations 2000 (NT) -- seat-neutral core.
--
-- The rules are written in the Act's own actors and terms: "an applicant", "the applicant's spouse or de facto partner",
-- "the Commissioner", "a person on whose application a first home owner grant was paid". Computations (the commencement
-- date, completion, the threshold, the amount, the periods and deadlines, interest) are functions. Where the text says
-- "must" or sets a deadline (ss 12, 14(3), 41(2), (3)), there is a regulative rule (DEONTIC). The applicant's questions are
-- in fhog-seat.l4, which IMPORTs this module and restates no rule.
--
-- EDITION: reprint REPF039 of the Act, as in force at 1 July 2026 (../../registers/source-bundle/
-- First-Home-Owner-Grant-Act-2000-NT-current-reprint-REPF039.txt); reprint REPF039R1 of the Regulations, as in force at
-- 1 July 2009 (../../../first-home-owner-grant-regulations-2000/registers/source-bundle/
-- First-Home-Owner-Grant-Regulations-2000-NT-current-reprint-REPF039R1.txt). Text quoted under the Northern Territory
-- copyright policy and the owner's ruling of 24 Oct 2026 (see SOURCE-LICENSE.md). Unofficial: not an official version.
--
-- NOT COVERED (an explicit answer, asserted): a commencement date before 1 January 2010 (s 53 keeps the Act as it stood
-- before the Revenue Legislation Amendment Act 2009 for those, and that text is not deposited; the 2009 boost amounts in
-- regs rr 5 and 6 are spent); a replacement contract or an earlier option under Part 5 (ss 54-56); an applicant whose facts
-- are not given.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 (NT) -- seat-neutral core`

§§ `Dates`

-- The stable l4 cannot compare two DATEs directly, so dates are compared by their serial day numbers.
GIVEN `a` IS A DATE, `b` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`on or after` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `a` AT LEAST DATE_SERIAL `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A DATE, `b` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`before` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `a` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A DATE, `b` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the earlier of` MEANS
    IF DATE_SERIAL `a` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A DATE, `b` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the later of` MEANS
    IF DATE_SERIAL `a` AT LEAST DATE_SERIAL `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `from` IS A DATE, `to` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`days from` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `to` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `from`

GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `d` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`days after` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `d` PLUS `n`)

-- "n months after" a day: the same day of the month n months on, or that month's last day where it is shorter
-- (29 February 2028 plus 12 months is 28 February 2029). READING: the Act does not say how a period of months is counted.
GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `d` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`months after` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY (min (DATE_DAY `d`) `days in the target month`) `target month` `target year`
    WHERE
        `month count` MEANS (DATE_YEAR `d` TIMES 12) PLUS (DATE_MONTH `d` MINUS 1) PLUS `n`
        `target month` MEANS (`month count` MODULO 12) PLUS 1
        `target year` MEANS (`month count` MINUS (`month count` MODULO 12)) DIVIDED BY 12
        `first of the target month` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 `target month` `target year`
        `first of the month after` MEANS
            IF `target month` EQUALS 12
            THEN DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 (`target year` PLUS 1)
            ELSE DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (`target month` PLUS 1) `target year`
        `days in the target month` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `first of the month after` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `first of the target month`

-- The days the Act turns on.
`1 July 2000`     MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2000
`1 January 2010`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2010
`4 December 2012` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 4 12 2012
`13 May 2014`     MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 13 5 2014
`1 January 2015`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2015
`28 April 2015`   MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 28 4 2015
`7 May 2019`      MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 7 5 2019
`1 October 2024`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2024
`1 October 2025`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2025
`1 October 2027`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2027

§§ `What is not covered`

DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    `a commencement date before 1 January 2010: s 53 keeps the Act as it was before the Revenue Legislation Amendment Act 2009, which is not deposited, and regs rr 5 and 6 (the 2009 boost amounts) are spent`
    `a replacement contract, or one made under an option or right granted before 1 October 2024: Part 5 (ss 54-56) is not encoded`
    `an applicant whose facts are not given`

-- s 53(2): "pre-amending Act transaction means an eligible transaction for which the commencement date is earlier than
-- the commencement of Part 2, Division 3 of the amending Act" (the Revenue Legislation Amendment Act 2009); s 53(1): "This
-- Act continues to apply in relation to a relevant application as if it had not been amended by Part 2, Division 3". The
-- endnotes give that Division's commencement as 1 January 2010. The unamended text is not deposited.
GIVEN `the commencement date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the commencement date is before 1 January 2010 (s 53)` IF
    `before` `the commencement date` `1 January 2010`

§§ `s 3 -- threshold amount`

-- s 3: "threshold amount, for an eligible transaction, means: (a) if the commencement date for the transaction is before
-- 4 December 2012 - $750 000; or (b) if the commencement date for the transaction is on or after 4 December 2012 -
-- $600 000." (Part 5 ss 54(3)(a) and 55(3)(b) fix it for replacement contracts; not encoded.)
GIVEN `the commencement date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the threshold amount (s 3)` MEANS
    IF `before` `the commencement date` `4 December 2012`
    THEN 750000
    ELSE 600000

§§ `s 4 -- home`

-- s 4: "A home is a building (affixed to land) that: (a) may lawfully be used as a place of residence; and (b) is, in the
-- Commissioner's opinion, a suitable building for use as a place of residence." (b) is the Commissioner's judgment: an
-- input, and the answer holds if the Commissioner is of that opinion.
GIVEN `the building is affixed to land and may lawfully be used as a place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner considers it a suitable building for use as a place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the building is a home (s 4)` IF
        `the building is affixed to land and may lawfully be used as a place of residence`
    AND `the Commissioner considers it a suitable building for use as a place of residence`

§§ `s 13 -- the kinds of transaction`

-- s 13(1)(a) "a contract ... for the purchase of a home"; (b) "a comprehensive home building contract" (s 3: a builder
-- undertakes to build a home "from the inception of the building work to the point where the home is ready for
-- occupation"); (c) "the building of a home ... by an owner builder" (s 3: an owner of land who builds a home, or has one
-- built, "without entering into a comprehensive home building contract"); s 13(7): a person who "purchases a building and
-- intends to use it as a place of residence on land in which the person has a relevant interest but on which it is not
-- situated at the time of purchase" is treated "as if the person were an owner builder".
DECLARE `Transaction kind` IS ONE OF
    `a contract for the purchase of a home`
    `a comprehensive home building contract`
    `the building of a home by an owner builder`
    `the purchase of a building to be placed on land in which the purchaser has a relevant interest`

GIVEN `kind` IS A `Transaction kind`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a contract for the purchase of a home` IF
    CONSIDER `kind`
    WHEN `a contract for the purchase of a home` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `kind` IS A `Transaction kind`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a comprehensive home building contract` IF
    CONSIDER `kind`
    WHEN `a comprehensive home building contract` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `kind` IS A `Transaction kind`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a transaction to which s 13(7) applies` IF
    CONSIDER `kind`
    WHEN `the purchase of a building to be placed on land in which the purchaser has a relevant interest` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `kind` IS A `Transaction kind`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is the building of a home by an owner builder, other than under s 13(7)` IF
    CONSIDER `kind`
    WHEN `the building of a home by an owner builder` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `s 4A -- new home`

-- s 4A(1): "A home is a new home if: (a) the home has not been previously occupied or sold as a place of residence; or
-- (b) all of the following apply: (i) the home is the subject of a contract for the purchase of the home; (ii) the sale of
-- the home is, under the A New Tax System (Goods and Services Tax) Act 1999 (Cth), a taxable supply as a sale of new
-- residential premises as defined in section 40-75(1)(b) of that Act; (iii) the home has not, since being renovated, been
-- occupied or sold as a place of residence; or (c) the Commissioner declares the home to be a new home under subsection
-- (2)." (3): "place of residence includes a building occupied as residential accommodation (regardless of the duration
-- of the occupation)" -- a hotel, serviced apartments or workers accommodation. The GST Act term is asked as a fact.
DECLARE `New home facts` HAS
    `the home has been previously occupied or sold as a place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `its sale is a taxable supply of new residential premises under s 40-75(1)(b) of the GST Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it has been occupied or sold as a place of residence since being renovated` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commissioner has declared it a new home under s 4A(2)` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `kind` IS A `Transaction kind`, `facts` IS A `New home facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the home is a new home (s 4A)` IF
        NOT (`facts`'s `the home has been previously occupied or sold as a place of residence`)
    OR  (    `it is a contract for the purchase of a home` `kind`
         AND `facts`'s `its sale is a taxable supply of new residential premises under s 40-75(1)(b) of the GST Act`
         AND NOT (`facts`'s `it has been occupied or sold as a place of residence since being renovated`))
    OR  `facts`'s `the Commissioner has declared it a new home under s 4A(2)`

§§ `s 5 and regs r 3 -- relevant interest`

-- s 5(2): "Each of the following is, subject to subsection (3), a relevant interest in land: (a) an estate in fee simple in
-- the land; (b) a life estate in the land approved by the Commissioner; (c) a perpetual lease of the land granted by the
-- Commonwealth or the Territory; (d) a leasehold interest ... granted by the Commonwealth or the Territory that may be
-- converted ... into an estate in fee simple; (e) an interest as purchaser under a contract for the purchase of an estate in
-- fee simple in the land by instalments; (f) a licence or right of occupancy granted by the Commonwealth or the Territory
-- that gives, in the Commissioner's opinion, ... reasonable security of tenure; (g) an interest as lessee or sublessee ...
-- under a long-term registered lease granted by the Commonwealth or the Territory where the term of the lease is 15 years
-- or more; (h) an interest as lessee or sublessee ... under a registered lease or sublease granted under section 19 or 19A
-- of the Aboriginal Land Rights (Northern Territory) Act 1976 (Cth) if the term of the lease is 15 years or more."
DECLARE `Interest in land` IS ONE OF
    `an estate in fee simple`
    `a life estate approved by the Commissioner`
    `a perpetual lease granted by the Commonwealth or the Territory`
    `a lease granted by the Commonwealth or the Territory that may be converted into an estate in fee simple`
    `an interest as purchaser of an estate in fee simple by instalments`
    `a licence or right of occupancy granted by the Commonwealth or the Territory that the Commissioner considers gives reasonable security of tenure`
    `an interest as lessee or sublessee under a registered lease granted by the Commonwealth or the Territory`
    `an interest as lessee or sublessee under a registered lease or sublease granted under s 19 or 19A of the Aboriginal Land Rights (Northern Territory) Act 1976`
    `none of these interests`

-- s 5(3): "(a) an interest is not a relevant interest at a particular time unless the holder of the interest has, or will
-- have within 12 months after that time (or a longer period allowed by the Commissioner), a right to immediate occupation
-- of the land; and (b) an interest is not a relevant interest in the hands of a person who holds it subject to a trust; and
-- (c) an equitable interest is not a relevant interest unless it is the interest of a person under a legal disability for
-- whom a guardian holds the interest in trust; and (d) an interest is not a relevant interest if the holder of the interest
-- is the lessor or sublessor under a lease or sublease mentioned in section 5(2)."
DECLARE `Interest facts` HAS
    `the interest` IS AN `Interest in land`
    `the term of the lease in years` IS A NUMBER
    `the holder has, or will have within 12 months or a longer period the Commissioner allows, a right to immediate occupation of the land` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the holder holds it subject to a trust` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is an equitable interest` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a guardian holds it in trust for the holder, a person under a legal disability` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the holder is the lessor or sublessor under a lease or sublease mentioned in s 5(2)` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `facts` IS AN `Interest facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the interest is of a kind listed in s 5(2)` IF
    CONSIDER `facts`'s `the interest`
    WHEN `an interest as lessee or sublessee under a registered lease granted by the Commonwealth or the Territory` THEN `facts`'s `the term of the lease in years` AT LEAST 15
    WHEN `an interest as lessee or sublessee under a registered lease or sublease granted under s 19 or 19A of the Aboriginal Land Rights (Northern Territory) Act 1976` THEN `facts`'s `the term of the lease in years` AT LEAST 15
    WHEN `none of these interests` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `facts` IS AN `Interest facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the interest is a relevant interest (s 5(2), (3))` IF
        `the interest is of a kind listed in s 5(2)` `facts`
    AND `facts`'s `the holder has, or will have within 12 months or a longer period the Commissioner allows, a right to immediate occupation of the land`
    AND NOT (`facts`'s `the holder holds it subject to a trust`)
    AND (    NOT (`facts`'s `it is an equitable interest`)
         OR  `facts`'s `a guardian holds it in trust for the holder, a person under a legal disability`)
    AND NOT (`facts`'s `the holder is the lessor or sublessor under a lease or sublease mentioned in s 5(2)`)

-- regs r 3(3): "relative, in relation to a person, means: (a) a spouse or de facto partner of the person; (b) the parents of
-- the person or the parents of a spouse or de facto partner of the person; (c) the grandparents of the person or the
-- grandparents of a spouse or de facto partner of the person; (d) a sibling of the person or of a spouse or de facto
-- partner of the person; (e) a child of the person; (f) a child of a child of the person; or (g) a spouse or de facto
-- partner of a person referred to in paragraph (d), (e) or (f)." "child ... includes an adopted child of the person and a
-- stepchild of the person."
DECLARE `Owner of the land` IS ONE OF
    `a spouse or de facto partner of the person`
    `a parent of the person, or of the person's spouse or de facto partner`
    `a grandparent of the person, or of the person's spouse or de facto partner`
    `a sibling of the person, or of the person's spouse or de facto partner`
    `a child of the person, including an adopted child or a stepchild`
    `a grandchild of the person`
    `a spouse or de facto partner of a sibling, child or grandchild in this list`
    `someone who is not a relative of the person`

GIVEN `owner` IS AN `Owner of the land`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner of the land is a relative of the person (regs r 3(3))` IF
    CONSIDER `owner`
    WHEN `someone who is not a relative of the person` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- regs r 3(1), in pursuance of s 5(4): where a person "(i) who has entered into a comprehensive home building contract on
-- land used solely or principally for farming purposes; or (ii) who has not entered into a comprehensive home building
-- contract begins building a home, or having a home built, on land used solely or principally for farming purposes; and
-- (b) the owner of the land has given permission for the person to occupy the home when it is completed, the
-- first-mentioned person has a relevant interest in the land." r 3(2): the same on "land owned by a relative of the person,
-- other than land used solely or principally for farming purposes", with the relative's permission. "farming purposes, see
-- section 4(1) of the Stamp Duty Act 1978": a borrowed term, asked as a fact. s 5(4): these count "even though the interest
-- may not conform with the above provisions".
DECLARE `Building on another's land` HAS
    `the person has entered into a comprehensive home building contract, or begun building a home or having one built, on the land` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the land is used solely or principally for farming purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the owner of the land` IS AN `Owner of the land`
    `the owner of the land has given permission for the person to occupy the home when it is completed` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `facts` IS A `Building on another's land`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person has a non-conforming relevant interest (regs r 3(1), (2))` IF
        `facts`'s `the person has entered into a comprehensive home building contract, or begun building a home or having one built, on the land`
    AND `facts`'s `the owner of the land has given permission for the person to occupy the home when it is completed`
    AND (    `facts`'s `the land is used solely or principally for farming purposes`
         OR  `the owner of the land is a relative of the person (regs r 3(3))` (`facts`'s `the owner of the land`))

GIVEN `interest` IS AN `Interest facts`, `building` IS A `Building on another's land`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person has a relevant interest in the land (s 5, regs r 3)` IF
        `the interest is a relevant interest (s 5(2), (3))` `interest`
    OR  `the person has a non-conforming relevant interest (regs r 3(1), (2))` `building`

§§ `s 6 -- spouses`

-- s 6(2): "a reference to an applicant's spouse or de facto partner ... is a reference to the applicant's spouse or de facto
-- partner at the commencement date of the eligible transaction". s 6(1): "If the Commissioner is satisfied that, at the
-- time of deciding an application ..., an applicant: (a) is married but not cohabiting with the person to whom the
-- applicant is married; and (b) has no intention of resuming cohabitation, the person to whom the applicant is married is
-- not to be regarded as the applicant's spouse." "De facto partner" is defined in the Interpretation Act (NT), not
-- deposited: asked as a fact.
DECLARE `Relationship at the commencement date` IS ONE OF
    `no spouse or de facto partner`
    `married`
    `a de facto partner`

GIVEN `relationship` IS A `Relationship at the commencement date`
      `the Commissioner is satisfied the applicant is married but not cohabiting and has no intention of resuming cohabitation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the applicant has a spouse or de facto partner (s 6)` IF
    CONSIDER `relationship`
    WHEN `married` THEN NOT (`the Commissioner is satisfied the applicant is married but not cohabiting and has no intention of resuming cohabitation`)
    WHEN `a de facto partner` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `ss 8-12A -- the eligibility criteria`

-- s 3: "Australian citizen, see section 4 of the Australian Citizenship Act 2007 (Cth)"; "permanent resident means: (a)
-- the holder of a permanent visa within the meaning of section 30 of the Migration Act 1958 ...; or (b) a New Zealand
-- citizen who holds a special category visa within the meaning of section 32 of the Migration Act 1958". The Commonwealth
-- terms are asked as facts; the Act's definition is worked out from them.
DECLARE `Citizenship or visa` IS ONE OF
    `an Australian citizen`
    `the holder of a permanent visa`
    `a New Zealand citizen who holds a special category visa`
    `none of these`

GIVEN `status` IS A `Citizenship or visa`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an Australian citizen or a permanent resident (s 3)` IF
    CONSIDER `status`
    WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 10(1): ineligible if the person "has been a party to an earlier application under this Act or a corresponding law;
-- and (b) a grant was paid on the application"; (2): "However, an applicant is not ineligible ... if: (a) the grant was
-- later paid back; and (b) any amount payable as a penalty or as interest was also paid". s 12A(1): ineligible, "Despite
-- sections 10(2) and 11(4)", if the person "was paid a grant on an earlier application ... for a home used as the
-- residence of the applicant, applicant's spouse or de facto partner" and "that transaction is not an eligible
-- transaction under ... section 13AA(1)(b), (c), (d) or (e) because the threshold amount is exceeded" (or the equivalent
-- under a corresponding law); (2): "even if the applicant ... repaid the amount of the grant".
DECLARE `Earlier grant` IS ONE OF
    `no grant was paid on an earlier application`
    `a grant was paid on an earlier application and has not been paid back with any penalty and interest`
    `a grant was paid on an earlier application and was paid back with any penalty and interest`
    `a grant was paid on an earlier application for a home used as a residence, on a transaction over the threshold amount`

-- s 11(1): ineligible if the person "held before 1 July 2000: (a) a relevant interest in residential property in the
-- Territory; or (b) an interest in residential property in a State or another Territory ... that is a relevant interest
-- under the corresponding law". (3): ineligible if the person "has, on or after 1 July 2000 and before the commencement
-- date ..., held an interest in property used at any time on or after 1 July 2000 as the residence of the applicant or the
-- applicant's spouse or de facto partner", being such an interest. (4), (5): the property is "taken not to have" been so
-- used if it "was the subject of an earlier application" and the grant was paid and repaid, or was not paid because the
-- Commissioner "did not exempt" the person from the age requirement. s 3: "residential property means land in Australia on
-- which there is a building lawfully occupied as a place of residence or suitable for occupation as a place of residence".
-- (2): a deferment of occupation because the property was leased is disregarded.
DECLARE `Earlier residential property` IS ONE OF
    `never held a relevant interest in residential property in Australia`
    `held a relevant interest in residential property in Australia before 1 July 2000`
    `held one from 1 July 2000, before the commencement date, in property used as a residence of the person or their spouse or de facto partner`
    `held one from 1 July 2000 only in property that was the subject of an earlier application whose grant was repaid, or was not paid for want of an age exemption`
    `held one from 1 July 2000 only in property that neither the person nor their spouse or de facto partner used as a residence`

-- One person's history, as ss 10, 11 and 12A ask it. s 10(3): "could have successfully applied for a first home owner
-- grant under this Act or a corresponding law in respect of an earlier transaction to which he or she was a party but did
-- not do so; or (b) could, assuming that he or she had then been an Australian citizen or a permanent resident, have
-- successfully applied". s 10(4): "received the first home owner discount under section 89AA of the Stamp Duty Act 1978
-- in relation to an earlier conveyance; and (b) the duty that would have been payable under that Act but for that
-- discount has not been paid."
DECLARE `History` HAS
    `earlier grant` IS AN `Earlier grant`
    `could have successfully applied for a grant on an earlier transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `received the first home owner discount on an earlier conveyance and the duty forgone has not been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
    `earlier residential property` IS AN `Earlier residential property`

-- One applicant. `has a spouse or de facto partner` is s 6, worked out by `the applicant has a spouse or de facto partner
-- (s 6)`. `will occupy the home as s 12 requires`: at the time of deciding, the Commissioner may pay "in anticipation of
-- compliance with the residence requirements" if satisfied each applicant intends to comply (s 17(3)); afterwards it is
-- whether the applicant did.
DECLARE `Applicant` HAS
    `is a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `age at the commencement date` IS A NUMBER
    `the Commissioner has exempted the applicant from the age requirement under s 8(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `citizenship or visa at the time of the application` IS A `Citizenship or visa`
    `own history` IS A `History`
    `has a spouse or de facto partner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `history of the spouse or de facto partner` IS A `History`
    `will occupy the home as the principal place of residence as s 12(2) requires` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commissioner has exempted the applicant from the residence requirement under s 12(3)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Criterion failed` IS ONE OF
    `s 8(1)(a): an applicant is not a natural person`
    `s 8(1)(b), (3): no applicant was 18 or over at the commencement date, and not every applicant has the Commissioner's exemption`
    `s 9: no applicant is an Australian citizen or permanent resident at the time of the application`
    `s 10(1), (2): a grant was paid to an applicant or their spouse or de facto partner on an earlier application and not paid back with any penalty and interest`
    `s 10(3): an applicant or their spouse or de facto partner could have successfully applied for a grant on an earlier transaction`
    `s 10(4): an applicant or their spouse or de facto partner received the first home owner discount and the duty forgone has not been paid`
    `s 11(1): an applicant or their spouse or de facto partner held a relevant interest in residential property before 1 July 2000`
    `s 11(3): an applicant or their spouse or de facto partner has held a relevant interest in residential property used as their residence`
    `s 12: an applicant will not meet the residence requirements and is not exempt`
    `s 12A: an earlier grant was paid for a home used as a residence on a transaction over the threshold amount`

DECLARE `Eligibility answer` IS ONE OF
    `eligible: every applicant meets the eligibility criteria (ss 7(1)(a), 8-12A)`
    `not eligible` HAS `because` IS A `Criterion failed`
    `eligibility not covered` HAS `because` IS A `Why not covered`

-- Per-history tests. Each criterion asks about "the applicant or the applicant's spouse or de facto partner".
GIVEN `h` IS A `History`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the history bars the person under s 10(1), (2)` IF
    CONSIDER `h`'s `earlier grant`
    WHEN `a grant was paid on an earlier application and has not been paid back with any penalty and interest` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `h` IS A `History`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the history bars the person under s 12A` IF
    CONSIDER `h`'s `earlier grant`
    WHEN `a grant was paid on an earlier application for a home used as a residence, on a transaction over the threshold amount` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `h` IS A `History`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the history bars the person under s 11(1)` IF
    CONSIDER `h`'s `earlier residential property`
    WHEN `held a relevant interest in residential property in Australia before 1 July 2000` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `h` IS A `History`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the history bars the person under s 11(3)` IF
    CONSIDER `h`'s `earlier residential property`
    WHEN `held one from 1 July 2000, before the commencement date, in property used as a residence of the person or their spouse or de facto partner` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- "the applicant or the applicant's spouse or de facto partner"
GIVEN `test` IS A FUNCTION FROM `History` TO BOOLEAN, `a` IS AN `Applicant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the applicant or their spouse or de facto partner is caught by` IF
        `test` (`a`'s `own history`)
    OR  (`a`'s `has a spouse or de facto partner` AND `test` (`a`'s `history of the spouse or de facto partner`))

GIVEN `h` IS A `History`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the history bars the person under s 10(3)` IF
    `h`'s `could have successfully applied for a grant on an earlier transaction`

GIVEN `h` IS A `History`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the history bars the person under s 10(4)` IF
    `h`'s `received the first home owner discount on an earlier conveyance and the duty forgone has not been paid`

-- s 8(1): "(a) a natural person; and (b) at least 18 years of age at the commencement date"; (2) the Commissioner may
-- exempt from (1)(b); (3): "If an application is made by joint applicants and one of the applicants complies with
-- subsection (1)(b), it is not necessary for the other or others to comply with that paragraph."
GIVEN `applicants` IS A LIST OF `Applicant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the age criterion is met (s 8(1)(b), (2), (3))` IF
        any (GIVEN `a` YIELD `a`'s `age at the commencement date` AT LEAST 18) `applicants`
    OR  all (GIVEN `a` YIELD `a`'s `age at the commencement date` AT LEAST 18 OR `a`'s `the Commissioner has exempted the applicant from the age requirement under s 8(2)`) `applicants`

-- s 9(1): "an Australian citizen or a permanent resident at the time of making the application"; (2): with joint
-- applicants, one is enough.
GIVEN `applicants` IS A LIST OF `Applicant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the citizenship criterion is met (s 9)` IF
    any (GIVEN `a` YIELD `an Australian citizen or a permanent resident (s 3)` (`a`'s `citizenship or visa at the time of the application`)) `applicants`

-- s 12(1): "An applicant ... must occupy the home ... as the applicant's principal place of residence unless the applicant
-- is exempt under subsection (3)(b) or (4)"; (4): "An applicant is exempt ... if: (a) the commencement date for the
-- transaction ... is on or after 28 April 2015; and (b) at least one other applicant to the application complies".
GIVEN `the commencement date` IS A DATE, `applicants` IS A LIST OF `Applicant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the residence criterion is met (s 12(1), (3)(b), (4))` IF
    all (GIVEN `a` YIELD
                 `a`'s `will occupy the home as the principal place of residence as s 12(2) requires`
              OR `a`'s `the Commissioner has exempted the applicant from the residence requirement under s 12(3)(b)`
              OR (    `on or after` `the commencement date` `28 April 2015`
                  AND any (GIVEN `b` YIELD `b`'s `will occupy the home as the principal place of residence as s 12(2) requires`) `applicants`))
        `applicants`

GIVEN `test` IS A FUNCTION FROM `History` TO BOOLEAN, `applicants` IS A LIST OF `Applicant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `some applicant or their spouse or de facto partner is caught by` IF
    any (GIVEN `a` YIELD `the applicant or their spouse or de facto partner is caught by` `test` `a`) `applicants`

-- s 7(1)(a): "the applicant or, if there are 2 or more of them, each of the applicants complies with the eligibility
-- criteria". The first criterion an application fails is the answer given.
GIVEN `the commencement date` IS A DATE, `applicants` IS A LIST OF `Applicant`
GIVETH AN `Eligibility answer`
`the eligibility of the applicants (ss 7(1)(a), 8-12A)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the commencement date is before 1 January 2010 (s 53)` `the commencement date`
        THEN `eligibility not covered` `a commencement date before 1 January 2010: s 53 keeps the Act as it was before the Revenue Legislation Amendment Act 2009, which is not deposited, and regs rr 5 and 6 (the 2009 boost amounts) are spent`
        IF NOT (all (GIVEN `a` YIELD `a`'s `is a natural person`) `applicants`)
        THEN `not eligible` `s 8(1)(a): an applicant is not a natural person`
        IF NOT (`the age criterion is met (s 8(1)(b), (2), (3))` `applicants`)
        THEN `not eligible` `s 8(1)(b), (3): no applicant was 18 or over at the commencement date, and not every applicant has the Commissioner's exemption`
        IF NOT (`the citizenship criterion is met (s 9)` `applicants`)
        THEN `not eligible` `s 9: no applicant is an Australian citizen or permanent resident at the time of the application`
        IF `some applicant or their spouse or de facto partner is caught by` `the history bars the person under s 12A` `applicants`
        THEN `not eligible` `s 12A: an earlier grant was paid for a home used as a residence on a transaction over the threshold amount`
        IF `some applicant or their spouse or de facto partner is caught by` `the history bars the person under s 10(1), (2)` `applicants`
        THEN `not eligible` `s 10(1), (2): a grant was paid to an applicant or their spouse or de facto partner on an earlier application and not paid back with any penalty and interest`
        IF `some applicant or their spouse or de facto partner is caught by` `the history bars the person under s 10(3)` `applicants`
        THEN `not eligible` `s 10(3): an applicant or their spouse or de facto partner could have successfully applied for a grant on an earlier transaction`
        IF `some applicant or their spouse or de facto partner is caught by` `the history bars the person under s 10(4)` `applicants`
        THEN `not eligible` `s 10(4): an applicant or their spouse or de facto partner received the first home owner discount and the duty forgone has not been paid`
        IF `some applicant or their spouse or de facto partner is caught by` `the history bars the person under s 11(1)` `applicants`
        THEN `not eligible` `s 11(1): an applicant or their spouse or de facto partner held a relevant interest in residential property before 1 July 2000`
        IF `some applicant or their spouse or de facto partner is caught by` `the history bars the person under s 11(3)` `applicants`
        THEN `not eligible` `s 11(3): an applicant or their spouse or de facto partner has held a relevant interest in residential property used as their residence`
        IF NOT (`the residence criterion is met (s 12(1), (3)(b), (4))` `the commencement date` `applicants`)
        THEN `not eligible` `s 12: an applicant will not meet the residence requirements and is not exempt`
        OTHERWISE `eligible: every applicant meets the eligibility criteria (ss 7(1)(a), 8-12A)`

§§ `s 13 -- eligible transaction, commencement, completion, consideration`

-- One case is one transaction (s 7(3): "Only one first home owner grant is payable for the same eligible transaction").
-- `the date the contract was made`: for a purchase or building contract, and under s 13(7) the date of the contract to
-- purchase the building. `the date laying the foundations commenced`: for an owner builder (s 13(5)(b)), or "another date
-- the Commissioner considers appropriate". `the consideration`: s 13(8) "the consideration for the purchase"; "the total
-- consideration payable for the building work"; "the actual costs to the owner of carrying out the work (excluding any
-- allowance for the owner builder's own labour)"; (8A) not "rent given for a lease or sublease mentioned in section
-- 5(2)"; (9) it "includes any GST payable in relation to the transaction". The unencumbered values (s 13AA(4): "the full
-- value of the home or interest (without regard to encumbrances)", including GST) matter only to a threshold-relevant
-- transaction. `an owner of the land`: the s 5 relevant interest, worked out by `the person has a relevant interest in the
-- land (s 5, regs r 3)`.
DECLARE `Transaction` HAS
    `kind` IS A `Transaction kind`
    `the date the contract was made` IS A DATE
    `the date laying the foundations commenced` IS A DATE
    `the home is in the Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the building is a home` IS A BOOLEAN
    `new home facts` IS A `New home facts`
    `the applicant is, or on completion will be, an owner of the land` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it replaces an earlier contract made, or is made under an option or right granted, before 1 October 2024` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an option or right granted before 1 July 2000 applies and the Commissioner has not declared it eligible` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the consideration` IS A NUMBER
    `the unencumbered value of the home` IS A NUMBER
    `the unencumbered value of the relevant interest in the land` IS A NUMBER
    `the land is wholly within the urban area` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 13(5): "The commencement date of an eligible transaction is: (a) in the case of a contract for the purchase or
-- construction of a home - the date when the contract is made; or (b) in the case of the building of a home by an owner
-- builder other than a transaction to which subsection (7) applies: (i) the date when laying the foundations for the home
-- commences; or (ii) another date the Commissioner considers appropriate ...; or (c) in the case of a transaction to which
-- subsection (7) applies - the date referred to in subsection (7)(b)" (the date of the contract to purchase the building).
GIVEN `t` IS A `Transaction`
GIVETH A DATE
`the commencement date (s 13(5))` MEANS
    IF `it is the building of a home by an owner builder, other than under s 13(7)` (`t`'s `kind`)
    THEN `t`'s `the date laying the foundations commenced`
    ELSE `t`'s `the date the contract was made`

GIVEN `t` IS A `Transaction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transaction's home is a new home` IF
    `the home is a new home (s 4A)` (`t`'s `kind`) (`t`'s `new home facts`)

-- s 13(6): "Subject to any qualifications prescribed by regulation" (none in the deposited Regulations), "an eligible
-- transaction is completed: (a) in the case of a contract for the purchase of a home, when: (i) the purchaser becomes
-- entitled to possession of the home under the contract; and (ii) if the purchaser is to obtain a registered title to the
-- land ... - the necessary steps to obtain registration of the purchaser's title have been taken; or (b) in the case of a
-- contract to have a home built - when the building is ready for occupation as a place of residence; or (c) [owner
-- builder] - when the building is ready for occupation as a place of residence; or (d) [s 13(7)] - when the event
-- referred to in subsection (7)(c) occurs" ("when the building is ready for occupation as a place of residence on land in
-- which the purchaser has a relevant interest").
DECLARE `Completion facts` HAS
    `the date the purchaser becomes entitled to possession of the home` IS A DATE
    `the purchaser is to obtain a registered title to the land` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date the necessary steps to obtain registration of the purchaser's title are taken` IS A DATE
    `the date the building is ready for occupation as a place of residence` IS A DATE

GIVEN `kind` IS A `Transaction kind`, `c` IS A `Completion facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the completion date (s 13(6))` MEANS
    IF `it is a contract for the purchase of a home` `kind`
    THEN IF `c`'s `the purchaser is to obtain a registered title to the land`
         THEN `the later of` (`c`'s `the date the purchaser becomes entitled to possession of the home`) (`c`'s `the date the necessary steps to obtain registration of the purchaser's title are taken`)
         ELSE `c`'s `the date the purchaser becomes entitled to possession of the home`
    ELSE `c`'s `the date the building is ready for occupation as a place of residence`

-- s 13(1)(a): a contract for the purchase of a home in the Territory "(i) if the contract was made before 1 January 2015 -
-- whether or not the home is a new home; or (ii) if the contract was made on or after 1 January 2015 but before 1 October
-- 2024 - only if the home is a new home; or (iii) if the contract is made on or after 1 October 2024 but before 1 October
-- 2025 - whether or not the home is a new home; or (iv) if the contract is made on or after 1 October 2025 - only if the
-- home is a new home".
GIVEN `the date the contract was made` IS A DATE, `new` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the home may be bought under s 13(1)(a)` IF
    BRANCH
        IF `before` `the date the contract was made` `1 January 2015` THEN TRUE
        IF `before` `the date the contract was made` `1 October 2024` THEN `new`
        IF `before` `the date the contract was made` `1 October 2025` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE `new`

-- s 13(1)(c): the building of a home by an owner builder "if the building work commences on or after 1 July 2000 and: (i)
-- the commencement date for the transaction is before 1 January 2015; or (ii) the commencement date ... is on or after
-- 1 January 2015 and one of the following applies: (A) the transaction is not a transaction to which subsection (7)
-- applies; or (B) if the transaction is a transaction to which subsection (7) applies - the home is a new home."
GIVEN `t` IS A `Transaction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a building bought to be moved fails s 13(1)(c)(ii)(B)` IF
        `it is a transaction to which s 13(7) applies` (`t`'s `kind`)
    AND `on or after` (`the commencement date (s 13(5))` `t`) `1 January 2015`
    AND NOT (`the transaction's home is a new home` `t`)

-- s 13AA(4): "threshold-relevant transaction means: (a) a transaction the commencement date of which is before 13 May
-- 2014; or (b) a contract for the purchase of a home if: (i) the commencement date ... is on or after 13 May 2014 but
-- before 1 January 2015; and (ii) the home is not a new home; or (c) a transaction that is the building of a home in the
-- Territory by an owner builder if: (i) the transaction is a transaction to which section 13(7) applies; and (ii) the
-- commencement date ... is on or after 13 May 2014 but before 1 January 2015; and (iii) the home is not a new home."
GIVEN `t` IS A `Transaction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a threshold-relevant transaction (s 13AA(4))` IF
        `before` `cd` `13 May 2014`
    OR  (    (`it is a contract for the purchase of a home` (`t`'s `kind`) OR `it is a transaction to which s 13(7) applies` (`t`'s `kind`))
         AND `on or after` `cd` `13 May 2014`
         AND `before` `cd` `1 January 2015`
         AND NOT (`the transaction's home is a new home` `t`))
    WHERE
        `cd` MEANS `the commencement date (s 13(5))` `t`

-- s 13AA(1): not an eligible transaction, for a threshold-relevant transaction: "(b) ... the consideration for the
-- transaction (including any GST payable in relation to it) is more than the threshold amount"; "(c) a contract for the
-- purchase of a home if ... the total of ... (A) the unencumbered value of the home; (B) the unencumbered value, at the
-- date the contract is made, of the relevant interest in the land on which the home is built or to be built" is more;
-- "(d) a comprehensive home building contract if ... the total of ... (A) the consideration for the transaction ...; (B)
-- the unencumbered value ... of the relevant interest in the land" is more; "(e) the building of a home by an owner
-- builder if ... the total of ... (A) the unencumbered value of the home; (B) the unencumbered value of the relevant
-- interest in the land", at the date the home is ready for occupation, is more.
GIVEN `t` IS A `Transaction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the threshold amount is exceeded (s 13AA(1)(b)-(e))` IF
        `it is a threshold-relevant transaction (s 13AA(4))` `t`
    AND (    `t`'s `the consideration` GREATER THAN `threshold`
         OR  `the total for the kind of transaction` GREATER THAN `threshold`)
    WHERE
        `threshold` MEANS `the threshold amount (s 3)` (`the commencement date (s 13(5))` `t`)
        `the total for the kind of transaction` MEANS
            IF `it is a comprehensive home building contract` (`t`'s `kind`)
            THEN `t`'s `the consideration` PLUS `t`'s `the unencumbered value of the relevant interest in the land`
            ELSE `t`'s `the unencumbered value of the home` PLUS `t`'s `the unencumbered value of the relevant interest in the land`

DECLARE `Transaction failed` IS ONE OF
    `s 4: the building is not a home`
    `s 13(1): the home is not in the Territory`
    `s 13(1)(b), (c), (2), (7): the applicant is not, and will not on completion be, an owner of the land (no relevant interest)`
    `s 13(1)(a)(ii), (iv): a contract made from 1 January 2015 to before 1 October 2024, or from 1 October 2025, for a home that is not a new home`
    `s 13(1)(c)(ii)(B): a building bought to be moved onto the land, from 1 January 2015, that is not a new home`
    `s 13AA(1)(a): an option or right granted before 1 July 2000, with no declaration by the Commissioner`
    `s 13AA(1)(b)-(e): a threshold-relevant transaction over the threshold amount`

DECLARE `Transaction answer` IS ONE OF
    `an eligible transaction (s 13(1))`
    `not an eligible transaction` HAS `because` IS A `Transaction failed`
    `the transaction is not covered` HAS `because` IS A `Why not covered`

-- s 13(1), (2), (7) and s 13AA. A contract for the purchase of a home is "a contract for the acquisition of a relevant
-- interest in land on which a home is built" (s 13(2)); a building contract is "by the owner of land in the Territory, or a
-- person who will on completion of the contract be the owner"; an owner builder is "an owner of land". Every kind needs
-- a home in the Territory. The 1 July 2000 start dates of s 13(1) fall inside the not-covered range.
GIVEN `t` IS A `Transaction`
GIVETH A `Transaction answer`
`whether the transaction is an eligible transaction (ss 13, 13AA)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the commencement date is before 1 January 2010 (s 53)` (`the commencement date (s 13(5))` `t`)
        THEN `the transaction is not covered` `a commencement date before 1 January 2010: s 53 keeps the Act as it was before the Revenue Legislation Amendment Act 2009, which is not deposited, and regs rr 5 and 6 (the 2009 boost amounts) are spent`
        IF `t`'s `it replaces an earlier contract made, or is made under an option or right granted, before 1 October 2024`
        THEN `the transaction is not covered` `a replacement contract, or one made under an option or right granted before 1 October 2024: Part 5 (ss 54-56) is not encoded`
        IF NOT (`t`'s `the building is a home`)
        THEN `not an eligible transaction` `s 4: the building is not a home`
        IF NOT (`t`'s `the home is in the Territory`)
        THEN `not an eligible transaction` `s 13(1): the home is not in the Territory`
        IF NOT (`t`'s `the applicant is, or on completion will be, an owner of the land`)
        THEN `not an eligible transaction` `s 13(1)(b), (c), (2), (7): the applicant is not, and will not on completion be, an owner of the land (no relevant interest)`
        IF     `it is a contract for the purchase of a home` (`t`'s `kind`)
                AND NOT (`the home may be bought under s 13(1)(a)` (`t`'s `the date the contract was made`) (`the transaction's home is a new home` `t`))
        THEN `not an eligible transaction` `s 13(1)(a)(ii), (iv): a contract made from 1 January 2015 to before 1 October 2024, or from 1 October 2025, for a home that is not a new home`
        IF `a building bought to be moved fails s 13(1)(c)(ii)(B)` `t`
        THEN `not an eligible transaction` `s 13(1)(c)(ii)(B): a building bought to be moved onto the land, from 1 January 2015, that is not a new home`
        IF `t`'s `an option or right granted before 1 July 2000 applies and the Commissioner has not declared it eligible`
        THEN `not an eligible transaction` `s 13AA(1)(a): an option or right granted before 1 July 2000, with no declaration by the Commissioner`
        IF `the threshold amount is exceeded (s 13AA(1)(b)-(e))` `t`
        THEN `not an eligible transaction` `s 13AA(1)(b)-(e): a threshold-relevant transaction over the threshold amount`
        OTHERWISE `an eligible transaction (s 13(1))`

§§ `s 14 -- the application period`

-- s 14(5): "An application may only be made within a period (the application period): (a) commencing on the commencement
-- date of the eligible transaction ...; and (b) ending 12 months after the completion of the eligible transaction". (6):
-- "However, the Commissioner has a discretion to allow an application to be made before or after the application period."
GIVEN `the completion date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the end of the application period (s 14(5)(b))` MEANS
    `months after` 12 `the completion date`

DECLARE `Application timing answer` IS ONE OF
    `within the application period: the application may be made (s 14(5))`
    `outside the application period: it may be made only if the Commissioner allows it (s 14(6))`

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, `the commencement date` IS A DATE, `the completion date` IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Application timing answer`
`whether an application may be made on the day (s 14(5), (6))` MEANS
    IF      `on or after` `the day` `the commencement date`
        AND NOT (`before` (`the end of the application period (s 14(5)(b))` `the completion date`) `the day`)
    THEN `within the application period: the application may be made (s 14(5))`
    ELSE `outside the application period: it may be made only if the Commissioner allows it (s 14(6))`

§§ `s 15 and regs r 4 -- all interested persons apply`

-- s 15: "(1) All interested persons must be applicants. (2) An interested person is a person who is, or will be, on
-- completion of the eligible transaction ..., an owner of the relevant home other than a person who is excluded from the
-- application of this section under the Regulations." regs r 4: excluded are "(a) the body corporate sole known as the
-- Chief Executive Officer (Housing) ...; (b) the owner of land in which a person has a relevant interest by virtue of
-- regulation 3(1) or (2)." s 3: an owner of a home is "a person who has a relevant interest in the land on which the home
-- is built".
GIVEN `the person is, or on completion will be, an owner of the home` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the Chief Executive Officer (Housing)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person owns land in which an applicant has a relevant interest only under regs r 3` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is an interested person who must be an applicant (s 15, regs r 4)` IF
        `the person is, or on completion will be, an owner of the home`
    AND NOT (`the person is the Chief Executive Officer (Housing)`)
    AND NOT (`the person owns land in which an applicant has a relevant interest only under regs r 3`)

§§ `s 18 -- amount of the grant`

-- s 18(4): "A home is an established home in the urban area if: (a) the land on which the home is or will be built is, as
-- at the commencement date for the eligible transaction, wholly within the urban area; and (b) the home is not a new
-- home." (6): "urban area means: (a) the Municipalities of Darwin, Palmerston and Litchfield and the Shire of Wagait; and
-- (b) Prescribed Area A described in the Schedule to the Northern Territory Rates Regulations 1971; and (c) the Darwin
-- Waterfront Precinct ...; and (d) any other area prescribed by regulation" (none in the deposited Regulations).
GIVEN `the land is wholly within the urban area` IS A BOOLEAN, `new` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the home is an established home in the urban area (s 18(4))` IF
    `the land is wholly within the urban area` AND NOT (`new`)

-- s 18(2)-(3F): the amount for s 18(1)(b), by commencement date. A dated table.
GIVEN `the commencement date` IS A DATE, `new` IS A BOOLEAN, `the land is wholly within the urban area` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount applying under s 18(2)-(3F)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `before` `the commencement date` `4 December 2012`
        THEN 7000
        IF `before` `the commencement date` `13 May 2014`
        THEN IF `established urban` THEN 12000 ELSE 25000
        IF `before` `the commencement date` `1 January 2015`
        THEN IF `established urban` THEN 12000 ELSE IF `new` THEN 26000 ELSE 25000
        IF `before` `the commencement date` `7 May 2019`
        THEN 26000
        IF `before` `the commencement date` `1 October 2024`
        THEN 10000
        IF `before` `the commencement date` `1 October 2025`
        THEN IF `new` THEN 50000 ELSE 10000
        IF `before` `the commencement date` `1 October 2027`
        THEN 50000
        OTHERWISE 10000
    WHERE
        `established urban` MEANS `the home is an established home in the urban area (s 18(4))` `the land is wholly within the urban area` `new`

DECLARE `Amount answer` IS ONE OF
    `the grant amount is` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `the amount is not covered` HAS `because` IS A `Why not covered`

-- s 18(1): "The amount of a first home owner grant is the lesser of the following: (a) the amount of consideration
-- actually paid for the eligible transaction; (b) the amount applying under subsections (2) to (3F)."
GIVEN `t` IS A `Transaction`
GIVETH AN `Amount answer`
`the amount of the grant (s 18)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the commencement date is before 1 January 2010 (s 53)` (`the commencement date (s 13(5))` `t`)
        THEN `the amount is not covered` `a commencement date before 1 January 2010: s 53 keeps the Act as it was before the Revenue Legislation Amendment Act 2009, which is not deposited, and regs rr 5 and 6 (the 2009 boost amounts) are spent`
        IF `t`'s `it replaces an earlier contract made, or is made under an option or right granted, before 1 October 2024`
        THEN `the amount is not covered` `a replacement contract, or one made under an option or right granted before 1 October 2024: Part 5 (ss 54-56) is not encoded`
        OTHERWISE `the grant amount is` (min (`t`'s `the consideration`) (`the amount applying under s 18(2)-(3F)` (`the commencement date (s 13(5))` `t`) (`the transaction's home is a new home` `t`) (`t`'s `the land is wholly within the urban area`)))

§§ `s 7 and s 17 -- is the grant payable`

DECLARE `Payability answer` IS ONE OF
    `payable` HAS `the amount` IS A NUMBER
    `not payable until the transaction is completed, unless the Commissioner pays it earlier (ss 7(1)(b)(ii), 17(2), (2A))` HAS `the amount` IS A NUMBER
    `not payable: an applicant does not meet the eligibility criteria` HAS `because` IS A `Criterion failed`
    `not payable: not an eligible transaction` HAS `because` IS A `Transaction failed`
    `not payable: an owner of the home has not joined in the application (s 15)`
    `payability is not covered` HAS `because` IS A `Why not covered`

-- s 7(1): "A first home owner grant is payable on an application under this Act if: (a) the applicant or, if there are 2
-- or more of them, each of the applicants complies with the eligibility criteria; and (b) the transaction for which the
-- grant is sought: (i) is an eligible transaction; and (ii) has been completed." s 17(2): the Commissioner "may authorise
-- the payment ... before completion ... if satisfied that: (a) there are special reasons for doing so; and (b) the
-- interests of the Territory can be adequately protected by conditions requiring repayment ... if the transaction is not
-- completed within a reasonable time"; (2A): likewise where conditions protect against s 13AA(1)(b)-(e). Whether the
-- Commissioner does is not known in advance, so before completion the answer says so.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      `t` IS A `Transaction`
      `c` IS A `Completion facts`
      `applicants` IS A LIST OF `Applicant`
      `every interested person is an applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Payability answer`
`whether the grant is payable (ss 7, 15, 17)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `whether the transaction is an eligible transaction (ss 13, 13AA)` `t`
    WHEN `the transaction is not covered` `why` THEN `payability is not covered` `why`
    WHEN `not an eligible transaction` `why` THEN `not payable: not an eligible transaction` `why`
    WHEN `an eligible transaction (s 13(1))` THEN
        CONSIDER `the eligibility of the applicants (ss 7(1)(a), 8-12A)` (`the commencement date (s 13(5))` `t`) `applicants`
        WHEN `eligibility not covered` `why` THEN `payability is not covered` `why`
        WHEN `not eligible` `why` THEN `not payable: an applicant does not meet the eligibility criteria` `why`
        WHEN `eligible: every applicant meets the eligibility criteria (ss 7(1)(a), 8-12A)` THEN
            IF NOT (`every interested person is an applicant`)
            THEN `not payable: an owner of the home has not joined in the application (s 15)`
            ELSE CONSIDER `the amount of the grant (s 18)` `t`
                 WHEN `the amount is not covered` `why` THEN `payability is not covered` `why`
                 WHEN `the grant amount is` `dollars` THEN
                     IF `on or after` `the day` (`the completion date (s 13(6))` (`t`'s `kind`) `c`)
                     THEN `payable` `dollars`
                     ELSE `not payable until the transaction is completed, unless the Commissioner pays it earlier (ss 7(1)(b)(ii), 17(2), (2A))` `dollars`

§§ `s 12 -- residence periods`

-- s 12(2): "That occupation of the home must: (a) start within 12 months after completion of the eligible transaction, or
-- a longer period approved under subsection (3)(a)(i); and (b) continue for a continuous period of: (i) if the
-- commencement date ... is on or after 1 October 2024 but before 1 October 2027 - at least 12 months, or a shorter period
-- approved under subsection (3)(a)(ii); or (ii) if the commencement date ... is before 1 October 2024 or on or after
-- 1 October 2027 - at least 6 months, or a shorter period approved". (3): approvals "If satisfied there are special
-- reasons"; s 30A: they may be given after the time has passed or the occupation has ceased.
GIVEN `the completion date` IS A DATE
      `the Commissioner has approved a longer period to start` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the end of the longer period approved` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date by which occupation must start (s 12(2)(a))` MEANS
    IF `the Commissioner has approved a longer period to start`
    THEN `the end of the longer period approved`
    ELSE `months after` 12 `the completion date`

GIVEN `the commencement date` IS A DATE
      `the Commissioner has approved a shorter period of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shorter period approved, in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the months of continuous occupation required (s 12(2)(b))` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Commissioner has approved a shorter period of residence`
        THEN `the shorter period approved, in months`
        IF `on or after` `the commencement date` `1 October 2024` AND `before` `the commencement date` `1 October 2027`
        THEN 12
        OTHERWISE 6

GIVEN `the day occupation started` IS A DATE, `months required` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the date until which occupation must continue (s 12(2)(b))` MEANS
    `months after` `months required` `the day occupation started`

§§ `s 21 -- death of an applicant`

-- s 21: "(1) An application ... does not lapse because an applicant dies before the application is decided. (2) ... (a) if
-- the deceased was one of 2 or more applicants and one or more applicants survive - the application is to be dealt with as
-- if the surviving applicants were the sole applicants; (b) in any other case - a first home owner grant, if payable on the
-- application, is to be paid to the estate of the deceased. (3) If a deceased applicant ... had not, by the date of death,
-- occupied the home ... but the Commissioner is satisfied that he or she intended to comply with the residence
-- requirements, the residence requirements are satisfied."
DECLARE `Death answer` IS ONE OF
    `the application does not lapse, and is dealt with as if the surviving applicants were the sole applicants (s 21(1), (2)(a))`
    `the application does not lapse; any grant payable is paid to the estate, and the residence requirements are satisfied (s 21(1), (2)(b), (3))`
    `the application does not lapse; any grant payable is paid to the estate (s 21(1), (2)(b))`

GIVEN `the deceased was one of 2 or more applicants and at least one survives` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deceased had not occupied the home by the date of death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner is satisfied the deceased intended to comply with the residence requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Death answer`
`what happens to the application on an applicant's death (s 21)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the deceased was one of 2 or more applicants and at least one survives`
        THEN `the application does not lapse, and is dealt with as if the surviving applicants were the sole applicants (s 21(1), (2)(a))`
        IF `the deceased had not occupied the home by the date of death` AND `the Commissioner is satisfied the deceased intended to comply with the residence requirements`
        THEN `the application does not lapse; any grant payable is paid to the estate, and the residence requirements are satisfied (s 21(1), (2)(b), (3))`
        OTHERWISE `the application does not lapse; any grant payable is paid to the estate (s 21(1), (2)(b))`

§§ `s 41 -- repayment: the required time, interest, penalty and charge`

-- s 41(1): the section "applies to a person on whose application a first home owner grant was paid if: (a) the person was
-- not entitled to the grant under section 7; or (b) the grant is paid before completion of a transaction and on completion
-- the consideration for it results in it not being an eligible transaction under section 13AA(1)(b) or (d); or (c) the
-- grant was paid in anticipation of compliance with the residence requirements and the person fails to comply with the
-- requirements; or (d) the Commissioner imposed a condition on the grant under section 5(5) or 20 and the person breaches
-- the condition; or (e) an overpayment of the amount to which the person was entitled occurs."
DECLARE `Repayment trigger` IS ONE OF
    `not entitled to the grant under s 7 (s 41(1)(a))`
    `paid before completion, and on completion the consideration takes it over the threshold (s 41(1)(b))`
    `paid in anticipation of the residence requirements, which are not complied with (s 41(1)(c))`
    `a condition imposed under s 5(5) or s 20 is breached (s 41(1)(d))`
    `an overpayment (s 41(1)(e))`

-- s 41(2A): "The required time is: (a) for non-entitlement ... - 30 days after the grant was paid; or (b) for ineligibility
-- mentioned in subsection (1)(b) - 30 days after the earlier of the following: (i) completion of the transaction; (ii) the
-- date on which it first became apparent that the transaction would not be an eligible transaction; or (c) for failure to
-- comply with the residence requirements ... - 30 days after the earlier of the following: (i) the date by which the
-- person was to have occupied the home; (ii) the date on which it first became apparent that the residence requirements
-- would not be complied with during the period allowed for compliance; or (d) for breach of a condition or an overpayment
-- ... - 30 days after the breach or overpayment occurred."
`the 30 days of s 41(2A)` MEANS 30

DECLARE `Repayment dates` HAS
    `the date the grant was paid` IS A DATE
    `the date of completion` IS A DATE
    `the date by which the person was to have occupied the home` IS A DATE
    `the date it first became apparent` IS A DATE
    `the date the breach or overpayment occurred` IS A DATE

GIVEN `trigger` IS A `Repayment trigger`, `dates` IS A `Repayment dates`
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the 30 days run from (s 41(2A))` MEANS
    CONSIDER `trigger`
    WHEN `not entitled to the grant under s 7 (s 41(1)(a))` THEN `dates`'s `the date the grant was paid`
    WHEN `paid before completion, and on completion the consideration takes it over the threshold (s 41(1)(b))` THEN `the earlier of` (`dates`'s `the date of completion`) (`dates`'s `the date it first became apparent`)
    WHEN `paid in anticipation of the residence requirements, which are not complied with (s 41(1)(c))` THEN `the earlier of` (`dates`'s `the date by which the person was to have occupied the home`) (`dates`'s `the date it first became apparent`)
    OTHERWISE `dates`'s `the date the breach or overpayment occurred`

GIVEN `trigger` IS A `Repayment trigger`, `dates` IS A `Repayment dates`
GIVETH A DATE
`the required time (s 41(2A))` MEANS
    `days after` `the 30 days of s 41(2A)` (`the day the 30 days run from (s 41(2A))` `trigger` `dates`)

-- s 41(12): "Interest accrues under this section at the statutory interest rate as in force from time to time." s 3:
-- "statutory interest rate, see section 35 of the Taxation Administration Act 2007": the "market interest rate" (the rate
-- prescribed for the financial year, or the RBA's average 90-day bank accepted bill yield for the previous May; an input)
-- plus the "premium interest rate", 8% from 1 July 2008 (TAA s 35(3)(b)).
`the premium interest rate (TAA s 35(3)(b))` MEANS 8%

GIVEN `the market interest rate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the statutory interest rate (TAA s 35)` MEANS
    `the market interest rate` PLUS `the premium interest rate (TAA s 35(3)(b))`

-- s 41(3)(a): "the person in default must pay interest on the amount in default from the date liability to make the
-- payment fell due until the date payment is actually made". READING: simple interest for each day, on a 365-day year,
-- as TAA s 34(3) calculates interest on a tax default ("on a daily basis"); s 41 does not say. The rate is taken as one
-- rate for the period.
GIVEN `the amount in default` IS A NUMBER
      `the market interest rate` IS A NUMBER
      `the days from the due date to payment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the interest on the amount in default (s 41(3)(a), (12))` MEANS
    (`the amount in default` TIMES `the statutory interest rate (TAA s 35)` `the market interest rate` TIMES `the days from the due date to payment`) DIVIDED BY 365

-- s 41(3)(b): the Commissioner "may, by notice in writing to the person: (i) state why the amount in default must be paid;
-- and (ii) require payment of the amount in default within 30 days after the date of the notice; and (iii) impose a penalty
-- equivalent to the amount in default"; (7): "The Commissioner may remit the whole or any part of a penalty or interest".
GIVEN `the amount in default` IS A NUMBER
      `the interest accrued` IS A NUMBER
      `the penalty and interest remitted` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`what the Commissioner's notice can require (s 41(3)(b), (7))` MEANS
    `the amount in default` PLUS `the interest accrued` PLUS `the penalty (s 41(3)(b)(iii))` MINUS `the penalty and interest remitted`
    WHERE
        `the penalty (s 41(3)(b)(iii))` MEANS `the amount in default`

-- s 41(5): "If a person who is liable to pay an amount under this section has an interest in the home for which the first
-- home owner grant was paid, the liability is an overriding statutory charge, within the meaning of the Land Title Act
-- 2000, on the person's interest in that home."
GIVEN `the person is liable to pay an amount under s 41` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has an interest in the home for which the grant was paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the liability is an overriding statutory charge on the person's interest in the home (s 41(5))` IF
    `the person is liable to pay an amount under s 41` AND `the person has an interest in the home for which the grant was paid`

-- s 41(11): "If a first home owner grant was paid on the application of 2 or more persons, the liability of those persons
-- under this section is joint and several." Each can be made to pay the whole.
GIVEN `the number of persons on whose application the grant was paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the liability is joint and several (s 41(11))` IF
    `the number of persons on whose application the grant was paid` AT LEAST 2

§§ `Regulative rules -- the applicant and the applicant's spouse or de facto partner`

-- Clock: days. Each rule says from which day it counts.
DECLARE `Grant party` IS ONE OF
    `the applicant`
    `the applicant's spouse or de facto partner`

DECLARE `Grant act` IS ONE OF
    `give the Commissioner the further information the Commissioner requires`
    `begin to occupy the home as the principal place of residence`
    `cease to occupy the home as the principal place of residence`
    `give the Commissioner written notice of the non-entitlement, ineligibility, failure, breach or overpayment`
    `pay the Commissioner the amount of the grant or overpayment`
    `pay the amount in default, the interest and the penalty`
    `pay the instalments the arrangement requires`

-- s 14(3): "An applicant and the applicant's spouse or de facto partner must provide the Commissioner with any further
-- information the Commissioner requires to decide the application." No period is stated: without a WITHIN the duty never
-- becomes a breach by time alone. Clock: from the Commissioner's requirement.
GIVEN `the applicant has a spouse or de facto partner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Grant party` `Grant act`
`s 14(3) -- the applicant and the spouse or de facto partner must give the further information the Commissioner requires` MEANS
    IF `the applicant has a spouse or de facto partner`
    THEN    (PARTY `the applicant`
             MUST  `give the Commissioner the further information the Commissioner requires`)
        RAND
            (PARTY `the applicant's spouse or de facto partner`
             MUST  `give the Commissioner the further information the Commissioner requires`)
    ELSE PARTY `the applicant`
         MUST  `give the Commissioner the further information the Commissioner requires`

-- s 41(2): "The person must, within the required time mentioned in subsection (2A): (a) give written notice to the
-- Commissioner of the non-entitlement, ineligibility, failure, breach or the overpayment; and (b) pay to the Commissioner
-- the amount of the grant or overpayment." (8): "A person who fails to comply with subsection (2) ... commits a regulatory
-- offence. Maximum penalty: 50 penalty units." (3)(a): from the due date, interest runs. Clock: day 0 is the day the 30
-- days of s 41(2A) run from (`the day the 30 days run from (s 41(2A))`); the deadline is day 30.
GIVEN `trigger` IS A `Repayment trigger`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Grant party` `Grant act`
`s 41(2), (2A) -- the person paid the grant must notify the Commissioner and repay within 30 days` MEANS
    CONSIDER `trigger`
    WHEN `not entitled to the grant under s 7 (s 41(1)(a))` THEN
            (PARTY `the applicant`
             MUST  `give the Commissioner written notice of the non-entitlement, ineligibility, failure, breach or overpayment`
             WITHIN `the 30 days of s 41(2A)`
             LEST  BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "s 41(2)(a), (2A)(a), (8): written notice of the non-entitlement was not given within 30 days after the grant was paid (a regulatory offence, up to 50 penalty units)")
        RAND
            (PARTY `the applicant`
             MUST  `pay the Commissioner the amount of the grant or overpayment`
             WITHIN `the 30 days of s 41(2A)`
             LEST  BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "s 41(2)(b), (2A)(a), (3), (8): the grant was not repaid within 30 days after it was paid; interest runs from then, and the Commissioner may require payment within 30 days with a penalty equal to the amount")
    WHEN `paid before completion, and on completion the consideration takes it over the threshold (s 41(1)(b))` THEN
            (PARTY `the applicant`
             MUST  `give the Commissioner written notice of the non-entitlement, ineligibility, failure, breach or overpayment`
             WITHIN `the 30 days of s 41(2A)`
             LEST  BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "s 41(2)(a), (2A)(b), (8): written notice of the ineligibility was not given within 30 days after completion or, if earlier, the day it became apparent (a regulatory offence)")
        RAND
            (PARTY `the applicant`
             MUST  `pay the Commissioner the amount of the grant or overpayment`
             WITHIN `the 30 days of s 41(2A)`
             LEST  BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "s 41(2)(b), (2A)(b), (3), (8): the grant was not repaid within 30 days after completion or, if earlier, the day it became apparent; interest runs, and a penalty equal to the amount may be imposed")
    WHEN `paid in anticipation of the residence requirements, which are not complied with (s 41(1)(c))` THEN
            (PARTY `the applicant`
             MUST  `give the Commissioner written notice of the non-entitlement, ineligibility, failure, breach or overpayment`
             WITHIN `the 30 days of s 41(2A)`
             LEST  BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "s 41(2)(a), (2A)(c), (8): written notice of the failure to meet the residence requirements was not given within 30 days (a regulatory offence)")
        RAND
            (PARTY `the applicant`
             MUST  `pay the Commissioner the amount of the grant or overpayment`
             WITHIN `the 30 days of s 41(2A)`
             LEST  BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "s 41(2)(b), (2A)(c), (3), (8): the grant was not repaid within 30 days of the failure to meet the residence requirements; interest runs, and a penalty equal to the amount may be imposed")
    OTHERWISE
            (PARTY `the applicant`
             MUST  `give the Commissioner written notice of the non-entitlement, ineligibility, failure, breach or overpayment`
             WITHIN `the 30 days of s 41(2A)`
             LEST  BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "s 41(2)(a), (2A)(d), (8): written notice of the breach of condition or overpayment was not given within 30 days after it occurred (a regulatory offence)")
        RAND
            (PARTY `the applicant`
             MUST  `pay the Commissioner the amount of the grant or overpayment`
             WITHIN `the 30 days of s 41(2A)`
             LEST  BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "s 41(2)(b), (2A)(d), (3), (8): the grant or overpayment was not repaid within 30 days after the breach or overpayment; interest runs, and a penalty equal to the amount may be imposed")

-- s 41(3)(b)(ii): the Commissioner's notice may "require payment of the amount in default within 30 days after the date of
-- the notice"; (c): "if the amount in default (together with interest and penalty) is not paid within 30 days from the date
-- of the notice, then, as from the end of that period, interest accrues on the penalty"; (8): failing to comply "with ... a
-- notice under subsection (3)" is a regulatory offence. (6): "The Commissioner may enter into an arrangement ... for
-- payment of a liability outstanding under this section by instalments"; its terms are the Commissioner's, so under an
-- arrangement the duty is to pay as it requires, with no period stated here. Clock: day 0 is the date of the notice.
`the 30 days of the notice (s 41(3)(b)(ii))` MEANS 30

GIVEN `an instalment arrangement has been made under s 41(6)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Grant party` `Grant act`
`s 41(3)(b), (c), (6) -- after the Commissioner's notice, the person must pay the amount in default, the interest and the penalty within 30 days` MEANS
    IF `an instalment arrangement has been made under s 41(6)`
    THEN PARTY `the applicant`
         MUST  `pay the instalments the arrangement requires`
    ELSE PARTY `the applicant`
         MUST  `pay the amount in default, the interest and the penalty`
         WITHIN `the 30 days of the notice (s 41(3)(b)(ii))`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "s 41(3)(b)(ii), (c), (8): the amount in default, the interest and the penalty were not paid within 30 days of the Commissioner's notice; interest now accrues on the penalty too, and failing to comply with the notice is a regulatory offence"

-- s 12(1), (2): the applicant "must occupy the home ... as the applicant's principal place of residence"; the occupation
-- "must: (a) start within 12 months after completion ...; and (b) continue for a continuous period" of 12 or 6 months
-- (`the months of continuous occupation required (s 12(2)(b))`). An applicant exempt under s 12(3)(b) or (4) owes nothing.
-- If the grant was paid in anticipation of compliance (s 17(3)), failure leads to s 41(1)(c) and the duty to notify and
-- repay; otherwise the residence criterion is simply not met and no grant is payable (s 7(1)(a)). Clock: day 0 is the
-- completion date; the first deadline is the day occupation must start by, and the second runs from the day occupation
-- started.
GIVEN `days from completion to the date by which occupation must start` IS A NUMBER
      `days of continuous occupation required` IS A NUMBER
      `the applicant is exempt from the residence requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the grant was paid in anticipation of compliance with the residence requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Grant party` `Grant act`
`s 12(1), (2) -- the applicant must start to occupy the home within 12 months of completion and continue for the required period` MEANS
    IF `the applicant is exempt from the residence requirement`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `the applicant`
         MUST  `begin to occupy the home as the principal place of residence`
         WITHIN `days from completion to the date by which occupation must start`
         HENCE
             PARTY `the applicant`
             SHANT `cease to occupy the home as the principal place of residence`
             WITHIN `days of continuous occupation required`
             LEST  `the consequence of not meeting the residence requirements`
         LEST  `the consequence of not meeting the residence requirements`
    WHERE
        `the consequence of not meeting the residence requirements` MEANS
            IF `the grant was paid in anticipation of compliance with the residence requirements`
            THEN `s 41(2), (2A) -- the person paid the grant must notify the Commissioner and repay within 30 days` `paid in anticipation of the residence requirements, which are not complied with (s 41(1)(c))`
            ELSE BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "s 12, s 7(1)(a): the residence requirements are not met, so the applicant does not comply with the eligibility criteria and no grant is payable"
